00:07:05.060 --> 00:07:05.320
Already.
确实。

158
00:07:05.320 --> 00:07:12.460
He gets the whole gang to visit her in the hospital and later discovers she may also have rabies.
他带着大家去医院探望她，后来发现她可能还患有狂犬病。

159
00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:19.780
Angela asks Dwight to give medicine to her cat, Sprinkles, while she visits Meredith in the hospital.
安吉拉在去医院探望梅雷迪思期间，拜托德怀特给她的猫“洒洒”喂药。

160
00:07:19.780 --> 00:07:27.060
But when Dwight returns, he announces that Sprinkles is dead, and he puts Sprinkles in the freezer.
但德怀特回来时宣布“洒洒”死了，并把它放进了冷冻室。

161
00:07:27.400 --> 00:07:29.320
In the freezer!
放进了冷冻室！

162
00:07:29.740 --> 00:07:31.540
Also, your television was on.
还有，你的电视开着。

163
00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:34.640
Yeah, my television was on, and Sprinkles is in the freezer.
没错，我的电视开着，而“洒洒”在冷冻室里。

164
00:07:35.240 --> 00:07:39.200
Meanwhile, everyone wants to know if Jim and Pam are dating.
与此同时，大家都想知道吉姆和帕姆是不是在约会。

165
00:07:39.360 --> 00:07:40.440
They insist they're not.
他们坚称没有。

166
00:07:40.540 --> 00:07:41.800
They say they're just friends.
他们说只是朋友。

167
00:07:41.800 --> 00:07:43.980
But Kevin is not convinced.
但凯文并不相信。

168
00:07:44.240 --> 00:07:47.020
Kevin really has a bee in his bonnet about it.
凯文对此事真是耿耿于怀。

169
00:07:47.420 --> 00:07:48.020
Yeah.
没错。

170
00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:50.120
Why does Kevin care so much?
为什么凯文这么在意？

171
00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:51.120
I don't know.
我不知道。

172
00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:52.140
He's obsessed.
他着魔了。

173
00:07:52.680 --> 00:08:03.240
Because this episode begins so dramatically, we felt like we needed to speak with the woman at the center of this episode.
因为这一集开场太戏剧性了，我们觉得有必要采访一下这一集的核心人物。

174
00:08:04.020 --> 00:08:04.620
Absolutely.
绝对有必要。

175
00:08:04.740 --> 00:08:09.260
We need to talk to Kate Flannery about getting hit by that car.
我们需要和凯特·弗兰纳里聊聊被车撞的那场戏。

176
00:08:09.760 --> 00:08:10.360
Yes.
没错。

177
00:08:10.360 --> 00:08:13.440
So, guys, Kate chatted with us.
所以，伙计们，凯特和我们聊过了。

178
00:08:13.580 --> 00:08:15.080
Sam, will you play the interview?
萨姆，能播放一下采访录音吗？

179
00:08:18.480 --> 00:08:22.120
Kate Flannery is here today, you guys, with her tiny teacup.
伙计们，凯特·弗兰纳里今天带着她的小茶杯来了。

180
00:08:24.240 --> 00:08:25.080
Hi, Kate.
嗨，凯特。

181
00:08:25.180 --> 00:08:25.820
How are you?
你好吗？

182
00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:26.360
I'm great.
我很好。

183
00:08:26.380 --> 00:08:27.160
How are you guys doing?
你们怎么样？

184
00:08:27.180 --> 00:08:28.280
It's so nice to see you.
见到你真高兴。

185
00:08:28.360 --> 00:08:30.380
Wait, we have to get a picture of you with that teacup.
等等，我们得给你和那个茶杯拍张照。

186
00:08:30.580 --> 00:08:31.660
Cody, will you take a picture?
科迪，能帮我们拍张照吗？

187
00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:33.940
It's not tiny.
它不小。

188
00:08:33.960 --> 00:08:35.680
It's a regular-sized teacup.
这是一个正常大小的茶杯。

189
00:08:35.680 --> 00:08:36.800
What's tiny about that?
哪里小了？

190
00:08:36.840 --> 00:08:37.660
I don't believe you.
我不信。

191
00:08:37.740 --> 00:08:38.320
It looks tiny.
看起来很小。

192
00:08:38.600 --> 00:08:39.160
It's regular.
它是正常的。

193
00:08:39.760 --> 00:08:40.860
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

194
00:08:40.860 --> 00:08:43.260
And you have a little cup and saucer.
而且你还有个小杯子和托盘。

195
00:08:43.860 --> 00:08:44.180
I do.
我有。

196
00:08:44.180 --> 00:08:44.920
Here's the thing, guys.
伙计们，重点是这个。

197
00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:48.040
Kate Flannery is one of the classiest gals.
凯特·弗兰纳里是最优雅的女士之一。

198
00:08:48.280 --> 00:08:50.060
Her home is spectacular.
她的家非常壮观。

199
00:08:50.280 --> 00:08:53.600
It is decorated like it's out of Architectural DigeSt.
装修得就像《建筑文摘》里出来的一样。

200
00:08:54.020 --> 00:08:56.020
Every little thing is amazing.
每一个小细节都令人惊叹。

201
00:08:56.020 --> 00:09:01.120
And I am not surprised at all that you look so put together and you're having your tea
看到你打扮得这么精致，还用着考究的茶杯和茶托喝茶，我一点也不惊讶。

202
00:09:01.120 --> 00:09:03.320
in a proper cup and saucer.
用着考究的茶杯和茶托喝茶。

203
00:09:03.440 --> 00:09:03.900
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

204
00:09:03.960 --> 00:09:04.160
Oh, wait.
噢，等等。

205
00:09:04.160 --> 00:09:06.200
But now I got to turn my phone off because someone's calling me.
但我现在得关掉手机，因为有人在给我打电话。

206
00:09:06.220 --> 00:09:06.270
Sorry, guys.
抱歉，各位。

207
00:09:06.270 --> 00:09:07.520
She's getting an important phone call.
她接到了一个重要电话。

208
00:09:07.920 --> 00:09:08.200
Sorry.
抱歉。

209
00:09:08.260 --> 00:09:08.860
Take it on air.
直播接听吧。

210
00:09:08.960 --> 00:09:09.420
Take it on air.
直播接听吧。

211
00:09:09.420 --> 00:09:10.020
Who is it?
是谁打来的？

212
00:09:10.120 --> 00:09:10.900
Let's talk to them.
让我们跟他们聊聊。

213
00:09:10.900 --> 00:09:13.260
I think it was a potential spam, so I hung up on them.
我觉得可能是骚扰电话，所以我挂了。

214
00:09:13.300 --> 00:09:13.680
I'm sorry.
抱歉。

215
00:09:13.940 --> 00:09:14.200
Oh, dang it.
噢，该死。

216
00:09:14.220 --> 00:09:17.360
I can't get locked in a timeshare just for you for the bit.
我可不能为了节目效果就让自己被分时度假房产套牢。

217
00:09:17.460 --> 00:09:18.080
I'm sorry, you guys.
抱歉，各位。

218
00:09:18.180 --> 00:09:18.520
I can't.
我做不到。

219
00:09:19.020 --> 00:09:20.280
It's so good to see you.
见到你真好。

220
00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:21.240
You don't understand.
你根本不懂。

221
00:09:21.240 --> 00:09:24.680
We spent every day together for nine years.
我们九年来每天都待在一起。

222
00:09:24.720 --> 00:09:25.540
I know.
我知道。

223
00:09:25.920 --> 00:09:26.820
Oh, my God.
天哪。

224
00:09:26.820 --> 00:09:27.520
I know.
我知道。

225
00:09:27.940 --> 00:09:30.540
It was so much like a real office job in that respect.
从那方面来说，这真的很像一份真正的办公室工作。

226
00:09:31.320 --> 00:09:31.800
It really was.
确实如此。

227
00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:33.580
Just like hours at our desks.
就像我们坐在办公桌前的时间一样。

228
00:09:34.100 --> 00:09:35.400
And the fluorescent light.
还有那荧光灯。

229
00:09:35.480 --> 00:09:35.840
Yes.
没错。

230
00:09:35.960 --> 00:09:37.740
I mean, that has a real effect on you.
我是说，那真的会对人产生影响。

231
00:09:37.840 --> 00:09:38.640
And the snacks.
还有零食。

232
00:09:38.880 --> 00:09:39.420
Come on.
得了吧。

233
00:09:39.540 --> 00:09:40.960
That was the best spread.
那里的零食种类最棒了。

234
00:09:41.220 --> 00:09:41.880
Oh, God.
天哪。

235
00:09:41.880 --> 00:09:43.800
We had the best, best food ever.
我们吃过最棒、最棒的食物。

236
00:09:43.900 --> 00:09:45.540
It's all my dad ever talked about.
我爸每次提起都津津乐道。

237
00:09:45.540 --> 00:09:49.380
All the years that he visited, and I would pepper him with questions about,
他来探班的那些年，我总是追着他问东问西，比如：

238
00:09:49.380 --> 00:09:51.480
so Steve Carell ate lunch with us today.
史蒂夫·卡瑞尔今天跟我们一起吃午饭了。

239
00:09:51.680 --> 00:09:52.280
Wasn't that great?
那不是很棒吗？

240
00:09:52.380 --> 00:09:54.740
And he was like, did you see the steak they had?
他就会说，你看到他们准备的牛排了吗？

241
00:09:55.640 --> 00:09:57.260
It was always about the food.
他总是三句不离吃的。

242
00:09:57.440 --> 00:09:58.200
Bill Kinsey.
比尔·金西。

243
00:09:58.560 --> 00:09:59.460
Oh, Kate.
噢，凯特。

244
00:09:59.740 --> 00:10:01.280
It's so good to see you.
见到你真好。

245
00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:02.820
And Jenna.
还有珍娜。

246
00:10:03.160 --> 00:10:03.760
You guys.
你们俩。

247
00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:04.680
You guys.
你们俩。

248
00:10:04.800 --> 00:10:10.180
Kate, we always like to start by asking people how they came to be on The Office.
凯特，我们总是喜欢先问问嘉宾是怎么加入《办公室》剧组的。

249
00:10:10.560 --> 00:10:13.240
I actually auditioned for the pilot for the part of Jan.
我其实试镜过试播集里简的角色。

250
00:10:13.540 --> 00:10:17.300
Allison Jones said, I think you're really right for this show, but I don't know if this
艾莉森·琼斯说，我觉得你真的很适合这部剧，但我不知道这

251
00:10:17.300 --> 00:10:17.720
is your part.
是你的角色。

252
00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:20.880
So clearly, they went a different way with Melora Harden.
显然，他们在梅洛拉·哈登身上选择了不同的方向。

253
00:10:21.460 --> 00:10:23.840
And lo and behold, you guys shot the pilot.
结果你瞧，你们拍了试播集。

254
00:10:23.940 --> 00:10:28.640
I remember that summer, I was doing a sketch show once a week that was timed.
我记得那个夏天，我每周都在做一个有时间限制的短剧节目。

255
00:10:28.800 --> 00:10:29.820
It was a two-minute sketch show.
那是一个两分钟的短剧节目。

256
00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:31.840
So literally, at two minutes, the lights would go out.
所以到了两分钟，灯光准时熄灭。

257
00:10:31.840 --> 00:10:38.280
It was this live show in Hollywood at this theater on Melrose with one of the Scholar
那是在好莱坞梅尔罗斯大街的一家剧院里演的现场秀，当时斯考勒

258
00:10:38.280 --> 00:10:40.900
brothers, Randy, was doing a sketch right before me.
兄弟之一的兰迪，就在我前面表演短剧。

259
00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:43.360
He's like, have you been watching that British show, The Office?
他说，你有看那个英剧《办公室》吗？

260
00:10:43.380 --> 00:10:44.340
I'm so obsessed with it.
我简直着迷了。

261
00:10:44.460 --> 00:10:46.000
He was like the first person to really tell me about it.
他是第一个真正向我推荐这部剧的人。

262
00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:47.060
I was like, yeah, I've seen a little bit.
我说，看过一点。

263
00:10:47.140 --> 00:10:48.520
He goes, you got to watch the whole thing.
他说，你一定要把整部剧看完。

264
00:10:48.880 --> 00:10:50.580
So I kind of got obsessed.
于是我也开始着迷了。

265
00:10:50.760 --> 00:10:54.460
And then come September, late August, early September, I had an audition.
到了九月，或者八月底九月初，我有个试镜。

266
00:10:54.580 --> 00:10:57.260
I couldn't make the first one because I was in Chicago with my aunt.
我没能参加第一次试镜，因为当时我在芝加哥陪我阿姨。

267
00:10:57.460 --> 00:10:58.320
And then I just came.
后来我赶回来了。

268
00:10:58.440 --> 00:11:00.740
I figured the part was going to get taken.
我以为那个角色肯定已经被别人拿走了。

269
00:11:00.940 --> 00:11:04.020
And they had another session a few days later.
几天后他们又安排了一场试镜。

270
00:11:04.020 --> 00:11:05.500
And I went in and I read.
我去了，然后进行了试读。

271
00:11:05.640 --> 00:11:07.920
And I remember Alison Jones said, no makeup.
我记得艾莉森·琼斯说，不要化妆。

272
00:11:08.160 --> 00:11:13.400
And usually in LA, you know, that means mascara, some foundation.
在洛杉矶，通常你知道的，那意味着要涂睫毛膏、打点粉底。

273
00:11:14.180 --> 00:11:15.620
It means something.
总得化点什么。

274
00:11:15.880 --> 00:11:17.920
It never really means no makeup, right?
从来不是真的不化妆，对吧？

275
00:11:18.080 --> 00:11:20.260
And they were like, literally, she literally had a box of tissues.
但他们是认真的，她真的拿了一盒纸巾。

276
00:11:20.380 --> 00:11:21.860
She's like, no makeup.
她说，不准化妆。

277
00:11:22.340 --> 00:11:23.300
Wipe it off.
擦掉。

278
00:11:24.400 --> 00:11:25.560
Get off, right?
卸掉，对吧？

279
00:11:26.060 --> 00:11:30.220
Anyway, and then I just remember there were a few actresses that I knew from Chicago that
总之，我记得当时有几个我认识的芝加哥女演员

280
00:11:30.220 --> 00:11:30.500
were there.
也在那里。

281
00:11:30.500 --> 00:11:31.840
And I felt like they booked everything.
我觉得她们什么角色都能拿到。

282
00:11:31.980 --> 00:11:33.140
I'm like, I'm never going to get this.
我想，我肯定没戏了。

283
00:11:33.440 --> 00:11:38.500
But I just remember that room was Ken Quapas and Greg and Alison Jones.
但我记得那个房间里有肯·夸帕斯、格雷格和艾莉森·琼斯。

284
00:11:38.900 --> 00:11:42.360
And I'm sure Paul Lieberstein was, I'm sure there were, you know, Mike Scher.
我肯定保罗·李伯斯坦也在，还有迈克·舒尔，你知道的。

285
00:11:42.380 --> 00:11:45.460
I'm sure all the producers were there, the writer producers.
我敢肯定所有的制片人都在，那些编剧兼制片人。

286
00:11:45.700 --> 00:11:49.140
It was like the most unique experience I think I'd ever had in an audition.
那是我经历过最独特的试镜体验。

287
00:11:49.440 --> 00:11:52.080
And then when I came out, I got home.
试镜出来后，我就回家了。

288
00:11:52.220 --> 00:11:55.900
And then Alison told me to go to Gower and do it again, do it one more time.
然后艾莉森让我去高尔街再试一次，再演一遍。

289
00:11:56.180 --> 00:11:57.840
And do less, less, less, do less.
而且要再收敛一点，再收敛一点，再收敛一点。

290
00:11:58.300 --> 00:12:02.220
And then by the time I got home from there, I found out that I got the part.
等我从那儿回到家时，就得知我拿到这个角色了。

291
00:12:03.120 --> 00:12:03.440
What?
什么？

292
00:12:03.600 --> 00:12:05.100
You booked it on the drive home.
你在开车回家的路上就定下来了。

293
00:12:05.120 --> 00:12:05.420
Isn't that weird?
这不是很神奇吗？

294
00:12:05.820 --> 00:12:06.300
Girl, way to go.
天哪，太棒了。

295
00:12:06.300 --> 00:12:08.300
And I didn't have a cell phone, so I didn't know till I got home.
当时我没有手机，所以直到回家才知道。

296
00:12:08.300 --> 00:12:09.480
That's every actor's dream.
那是每个演员的梦想。

297
00:12:09.620 --> 00:12:11.680
You didn't have a cell phone, so you didn't know.
你没有手机，所以你当时不知道。

298
00:12:11.840 --> 00:12:13.280
Those were the days, man.
那真是个好时代啊，伙计。

299
00:12:13.540 --> 00:12:14.580
Like, you know what?
就像，你知道吗？

300
00:12:14.780 --> 00:12:16.380
You couldn't, they couldn't get a hold of you.
你没法，他们没法联系到你。

301
00:12:16.560 --> 00:12:17.960
You found out at home.
你在家里发现的。

302
00:12:18.660 --> 00:12:20.760
I was playing hard to get on the drive home.
我在开车回家的路上故意装矜持。

303
00:12:20.760 --> 00:12:21.180
Wow.
哇。

304
00:12:21.600 --> 00:12:23.840
Well, Kate, I was so excited.
凯特，我当时太兴奋了。

305
00:12:24.120 --> 00:12:28.480
Because when you walked on the set that day, Kate and I had been doing an improv show called
因为那天你走进片场时，我和凯特一直在做一个即兴表演节目，叫

306
00:12:28.480 --> 00:12:29.360
Bitch Planet.
《贱人星球》。

307
00:12:29.540 --> 00:12:30.540
All chick improv.
全女性即兴表演。

308
00:12:30.820 --> 00:12:31.880
All chick improv.
全女性即兴表演。

309
00:12:32.240 --> 00:12:34.200
And we'd been doing that for years.
我们做了好几年了。

310
00:12:34.200 --> 00:12:39.380
And then all of a sudden, my good friend was going to be sitting, like, right behind
突然之间，我的好朋友就要坐在我身后，

311
00:12:39.380 --> 00:12:40.240
me for years.
好几年了。

312
00:12:40.360 --> 00:12:41.400
That was just amazing.
那真是太神奇了。

313
00:12:41.800 --> 00:12:42.540
Who knew?
谁能想到呢？

314
00:12:42.660 --> 00:12:46.260
When four people were in our audience on a Sunday night for our show.
当时周日晚上我们的观众只有四个人。

315
00:12:46.300 --> 00:12:47.180
At 10 o'clock.
在十点钟的时候。

316
00:12:47.940 --> 00:12:50.880
Kate, do you remember what your audition scene was?
凯特，你还记得你的试镜片段是什么吗？

317
00:12:51.040 --> 00:12:54.100
Yeah, it was from the Alliance.
记得，是《联盟》里的那段。

318
00:12:54.100 --> 00:13:00.860
It was the whole reaction to the surprise party and Michael reading the birthday card
就是对惊喜派对的全部反应，还有迈克尔读生日贺卡，

319
00:13:00.860 --> 00:13:03.020
and insulting Meredith like crazy.
疯狂地侮辱梅雷迪思。

320
00:13:03.360 --> 00:13:04.520
Yes, amazing.
没错，太棒了。

321
00:13:05.180 --> 00:13:06.380
Yeah, it was so awesome.
是啊，太棒了。

322
00:13:06.640 --> 00:13:07.220
So awesome.
太棒了。

