我不会坐在别人的桌子上。

484
00:19:43.680 --> 00:19:44.140
No.
不会。

485
00:19:44.560 --> 00:19:47.740
Like I would never just go sit down in Phyllis's chair.
我绝不会去坐在菲利斯的椅子上。

486
00:19:47.940 --> 00:19:48.180
No.
不会。

487
00:19:49.000 --> 00:19:49.400
Right?
对吧？

488
00:19:50.020 --> 00:19:51.420
That was like her space.
那是她的空间。

489
00:19:52.000 --> 00:19:55.460
Sometimes Rain would sit at my desk to talk fantasy football with Brian.
有时雷恩会坐在我的桌子上和布莱恩聊梦幻足球。

490
00:19:55.820 --> 00:19:56.180
Right.
没错。

491
00:19:56.320 --> 00:19:58.500
And I would have to come kick him out of my seat.
我不得不去把他从我的座位上赶走。

492
00:19:59.740 --> 00:20:03.460
But I just had such respect for the process.
但我对这个过程非常尊重。

493
00:20:03.680 --> 00:20:06.720
I just feel like the focus was always in the right place for our show.
我觉得我们的剧集总是把焦点放在正确的地方。

494
00:20:07.180 --> 00:20:07.400
Yeah.
是啊。

495
00:20:07.800 --> 00:20:08.240
Yeah.
是啊。

496
00:20:08.560 --> 00:20:11.540
And I feel like I didn't always have a lot of lines, obviously.
而且我觉得我显然并不总是有很多台词。

497
00:20:11.720 --> 00:20:17.520
But I feel like there was something that I felt like I was kind of holding the space for the reality that we were in.
但我感觉我好像在为我们所处的现实守护着那个空间。

498
00:20:17.600 --> 00:20:18.920
And that was very important to me.
这对我很重要。

499
00:20:18.980 --> 00:20:20.560
I was always very conscious of that.
我一直对此非常有意识。

500
00:20:20.780 --> 00:20:27.400
Well, we are super excited to talk to you about this amazing stunt that you did in this episode.
好吧，我们非常兴奋能和你聊聊你在这一集中完成的那个惊人的特技。

501
00:20:27.680 --> 00:20:29.740
I mean, holy cow, Kate.
我的天哪，凯特。

502
00:20:30.420 --> 00:20:32.340
You get hit by a car.
你被车撞了。

503
00:20:32.540 --> 00:20:34.360
You get hit by a car.
你被车撞了。

504
00:20:34.980 --> 00:20:38.200
What was your first thought when you read this episode?
你读到这一集剧本时，第一个念头是什么？

505
00:20:38.460 --> 00:20:40.540
I literally said, does she live?
我当时真的在想，她活下来了吗？

506
00:20:40.840 --> 00:20:42.240
I literally said, does Meredith live?
我当时真的在想，梅雷迪思活下来了吗？

507
00:20:42.360 --> 00:20:43.460
I said it right away.
我脱口而出就是这句话。

508
00:20:43.640 --> 00:20:51.760
And then like I've been reading later that like there's been articles saying that one of the writers decided that, you know, they wanted to pitch that Meredith didn't live.
后来我读到一些文章说，有位编剧曾提议让梅雷迪思死掉。

509
00:20:51.880 --> 00:20:53.180
And then they thought that was too dark.
但他们觉得那样太黑暗了。

510
00:20:53.460 --> 00:20:56.980
Greg thought it was too dark for Michael to have killed one of the employees.
格雷格觉得让迈克尔撞死一名员工太黑暗了。

511
00:20:56.980 --> 00:20:57.760
Oh, my God.
天哪。

512
00:20:57.800 --> 00:20:57.940
Yeah.
是啊。

513
00:20:57.960 --> 00:20:59.140
How do you come back from that?
那种情况下怎么收场呢？

514
00:20:59.360 --> 00:21:00.300
Yeah, I'm not sure.
是啊，我也不确定。

515
00:21:00.460 --> 00:21:00.800
I'm not sure.
我也不确定。

516
00:21:00.880 --> 00:21:06.200
But I was like, but I remember like I was so conscious of it because I was like, I know this isn't a soap opera, like this could be it.
但我记得当时我特别在意，因为我知道这不是肥皂剧，这可能就是结局了。

517
00:21:06.340 --> 00:21:13.940
But the first time we shot it, literally they played it almost like Meredith was a speed bump that he just like went over.
但第一次拍摄时，他们拍得简直就像梅雷迪思只是个减速带，他直接开了过去。

518
00:21:14.240 --> 00:21:17.740
Because like you were laying on the ground and he rolled over you.
因为你当时躺在地上，他从你身上碾了过去。

519
00:21:17.740 --> 00:21:19.200
I was underneath the wheel, literally.
我当时真的就在车轮底下。

520
00:21:19.480 --> 00:21:25.540
We finished shooting the episode and then I think two weeks later, Dave Rogers, our Emmy winning editor,
我们拍完那一集，大概两周后，我们的艾美奖获奖剪辑师戴夫·罗杰斯，

521
00:21:25.840 --> 00:21:33.980
had an idea for an insert shot that he thought was so much more interesting than what we had shot, which was Meredith hitting the glass.
他想到了一个插入镜头，觉得比我们拍的梅雷迪思撞上挡风玻璃的效果更有意思。

522
00:21:34.460 --> 00:21:39.960
And he asked our UPM, Kent Zbornak, to try it out and show it to me.
他让我们的制片经理肯特·兹博纳克去尝试一下，并展示给我看。

523
00:21:40.100 --> 00:21:40.940
He's like, Kent did it.
他说，肯特做到了。

524
00:21:41.000 --> 00:21:41.580
Do you think he'd do it?
你觉得他会愿意做吗？

525
00:21:41.700 --> 00:21:44.880
I mean, he obviously did not know me because I would have said yes.
我是说，他显然不了解我，因为我肯定会答应的。

526
00:21:45.020 --> 00:21:46.300
I totally would have said yes.
我绝对会答应的。

527
00:21:46.300 --> 00:21:48.160
I was going to say, you would say yes.
我正想说，你肯定会答应。

528
00:21:48.320 --> 00:21:48.540
I would have.
我会的。

529
00:21:48.580 --> 00:21:57.860
But season one, I remember Greg, there was a shot of Dwight and Michael dressed like Crockett and Tubbs from Miami Vice from the Halloween party.
但第一季的时候，我记得格雷格拍过一个镜头，德怀特和迈克尔打扮成《迈阿密风云》里的克罗克特和塔布斯，那是万圣节派对上的造型。

530
00:21:57.980 --> 00:21:58.380
Do you remember that?
你还记得吗？

531
00:21:58.540 --> 00:21:58.820
Yes.
记得。

532
00:21:59.000 --> 00:21:59.240
Yeah.
是啊。

533
00:21:59.580 --> 00:22:01.420
And they had me dress up like Madonna.
他们让我打扮成麦当娜。

534
00:22:01.660 --> 00:22:06.460
And I remember it was like, it was like maybe my second week there and I was like, oh, okay, I'll be Madonna, whatever.
我记得那大概是我在那儿的第二周，我就想，哦，好吧，演麦当娜就演吧，无所谓。

535
00:22:06.680 --> 00:22:08.100
And like they really went for it.
他们真的全力以赴了。

536
00:22:08.180 --> 00:22:10.620
I mean, I was like 1987 Madonna.
我是说，我当时就是1987年版的麦当娜。

537
00:22:10.720 --> 00:22:12.160
I was wearing like a bustier.
我穿着紧身胸衣。

538
00:22:12.320 --> 00:22:12.740
It was nuts.
太疯狂了。

539
00:22:12.940 --> 00:22:13.780
I was just in the background.
我当时只是在背景里。

540
00:22:14.280 --> 00:22:16.500
And I thought there was something about that.
我觉得那件事有点特别。

541
00:22:16.620 --> 00:22:20.100
It was like my responsibility to do whatever as full out as possible.
就像我有责任尽我所能做到极致。

542
00:22:20.280 --> 00:22:20.640
I don't know.
我不知道。

543
00:22:20.740 --> 00:22:24.100
I was like kind of up for anything because I remember Greg saying, is it okay if you do this?
我当时什么都愿意尝试，因为我记得格雷格问我，你做这个没问题吧？

544
00:22:24.180 --> 00:22:25.000
And I was like, sure.
我说，没问题。

545
00:22:25.240 --> 00:22:26.100
Like, of course.
当然没问题。

546
00:22:26.100 --> 00:22:29.560
So that started the whole Meredith saga.
所以那开启了整个梅雷迪思的传奇。

547
00:22:29.820 --> 00:22:32.100
Being full Madonna started it all.
全套麦当娜造型开启了一切。

548
00:22:33.080 --> 00:22:39.000
But I actually felt like it was so much fun to do the physical comedy because I have such a good time doing it.
但我其实觉得做肢体喜剧特别有趣，因为我乐在其中。

549
00:22:39.020 --> 00:22:41.620
I mean, I've always had a good time doing that my whole career.
我是说，我整个职业生涯一直都很享受做这些。

550
00:22:41.620 --> 00:22:44.600
But like this was so up another level for sure.
但这次绝对是提升到了另一个高度。

551
00:22:44.860 --> 00:22:47.780
So literally when we went to shoot it, we had to shoot it again.
所以实际上当我们去拍摄的时候，我们不得不重拍了一次。

552
00:22:47.920 --> 00:22:49.060
And Steve wasn't available.
而且史蒂夫当时没空。

553
00:22:49.060 --> 00:22:58.820
So Dan Beals, who was our PA, who was so young at the time, he had Steve's jacket on and shirt.
所以我们的制片助理丹·比尔斯，他当时还很年轻，就穿上了史蒂夫的夹克和衬衫。

554
00:22:58.820 --> 00:23:01.740
So it was his hand that they would cut from.
所以他们剪辑时用的是他的手。

555
00:23:01.820 --> 00:23:04.240
And it's such a quick swipe.
而且那只是一个很快的扫过镜头。

556
00:23:04.420 --> 00:23:05.580
Like, you know.
就像，你知道的。

557
00:23:05.800 --> 00:23:08.020
So wait, Dan was driving?
等等，所以是丹在开车？

558
00:23:08.500 --> 00:23:10.080
Well, he was just in the car.
嗯，他只是在车里。

559
00:23:10.400 --> 00:23:11.060
In the car.
在车里。

560
00:23:11.200 --> 00:23:11.480
The car was stationary.
车是静止的。

561
00:23:11.860 --> 00:23:14.000
I started in the center of the hood.
我从引擎盖中间开始。

562
00:23:14.000 --> 00:23:18.260
I had to roll up to the glass and then roll off the car onto a giant mat.
我得滚到挡风玻璃上，然后再从车上滚到一个巨大的垫子上。

563
00:23:19.100 --> 00:23:23.600
So you sort of had to, like, with force, roll into that windshield on your own.
所以你得用力，自己滚到挡风玻璃上。

564
00:23:23.740 --> 00:23:29.180
You sort of slammed your body into the windshield and then slowly rolled off of it onto a mat in the parking lot.
你得把身体猛地撞向挡风玻璃，然后慢慢滚下来，落到停车场的一个垫子上。

565
00:23:29.200 --> 00:23:29.480
Yes.
是的。

566
00:23:29.600 --> 00:23:38.840
And I remember after, like, the fourth take or fifth take, Greg took me aside and we went to the back where the warehouse entrance is in that alley where we shot, like,
我记得拍了四五次之后，格雷格把我拉到一边，我们去了拍摄地那条小巷的仓库入口后面，就是，

567
00:23:38.840 --> 00:23:41.320
where the bird, you know, where they had the bird funeral, you know, the alley.
就是那只鸟，你知道的，他们举行鸟葬礼的那条小巷。

568
00:23:41.320 --> 00:23:41.940
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
对，对，对。

569
00:23:42.640 --> 00:23:43.700
He's like, okay, come with me.
他说，好吧，跟我来。

570
00:23:44.000 --> 00:23:45.040
And do some jumping jacks.
然后做些开合跳。

571
00:23:45.140 --> 00:23:47.340
He was, like, doing jumping jacks with me just to get me really loose.
他陪我一起做开合跳，只是为了让我彻底放松下来。

572
00:23:47.420 --> 00:23:48.840
I love Greg so much.
我太爱格雷格了。

573
00:23:49.200 --> 00:23:50.540
That's so Greg, by the way.
顺便说一句，这太格雷格了。

574
00:23:50.740 --> 00:23:51.800
He's, like, the greateSt.
他真是太棒了。

575
00:23:52.040 --> 00:23:52.520
It's funny.
真有趣。

576
00:23:52.580 --> 00:23:58.820
I just recently saw Dave Rogers sent me an outtake, another take that they didn't use.
我最近看到戴夫·罗杰斯给我发了一个花絮，是他们没用上的另一个镜头。

577
00:23:58.820 --> 00:24:02.340
And I actually did an extra spin in there, which I actually thought was a little funnier.
我其实在里面多转了一圈，我觉得那个其实更有趣一点。

578
00:24:02.420 --> 00:24:04.280
But I'm just so used to watching the one thing.
但我已经习惯看正片里的那个了。

579
00:24:04.340 --> 00:24:05.460
I think it just caught me by surprise.
我想它只是让我感到意外。

580
00:24:06.220 --> 00:24:12.680
So wait, there is a take of you out in the universe where you roll, you flip forward twice into the windshield?
等等，所以在这个世界上还存在一个镜头，是你滚过去，然后在挡风玻璃上翻了两个跟头？

581
00:24:12.680 --> 00:24:15.420
No, once in the windshield, but then I flip twice off the car.
不，撞到挡风玻璃是一次，但我从车上滚下来时翻了两个跟头。

582
00:24:15.660 --> 00:24:16.060
Oh.
哦。

583
00:24:16.180 --> 00:24:18.060
So it's like, like, it's insane.
所以这看起来，简直太疯狂了。

584
00:24:18.220 --> 00:24:18.660
It's insane.
太疯狂了。

585
00:24:19.500 --> 00:24:25.000
Well, guys, at 53 seconds, you can see Kate's face up against the windshield.
伙计们，在53秒的时候，你们可以看到凯特的脸贴在挡风玻璃上。

586
00:24:26.400 --> 00:24:34.220
And I'm telling you, after we shot that, I remember they were using it in the promos for the episode because it was the first episode of season four, Fun Run.
我告诉你们，拍完那个之后，我记得他们把它用在剧集的宣传片里了，因为那是第四季的第一集，《欢乐跑》。

587
00:24:34.420 --> 00:24:39.000
I remember Joaquin Phoenix canceled at the last minute for The Tonight Show.
我记得杰昆·菲尼克斯在最后一刻取消了《今夜秀》的通告。

588
00:24:39.160 --> 00:24:41.800
So they asked me basically because of the promo.
所以他们基本上是因为那个宣传片才邀请了我。

589
00:24:41.960 --> 00:24:42.520
It was so much fun.
那真的太好玩了。

590
00:24:42.600 --> 00:24:44.380
Like, they actually want to be on The Tonight Show.
就像，他们竟然真的想上《今夜秀》一样。

591
00:24:44.440 --> 00:24:45.520
So that was the first time I did that.
所以那是我第一次上那个节目。

592
00:24:45.580 --> 00:24:46.620
That was so awesome.
那真是太棒了。

593
00:24:46.620 --> 00:24:49.840
Well, Kate, Kate, you're just like a rock star.
凯特，凯特，你简直就是个摇滚明星。

594
00:24:49.980 --> 00:24:57.560
I mean, I have to ask you, though, if you're rolling with force into a windshield over and over and rolling off, were you sore?
不过我得问你，如果你反复用力滚向挡风玻璃再滚下来，你会觉得酸痛吗？

595
00:24:58.140 --> 00:24:59.000
Did you, like...
你有没有……

596
00:24:59.000 --> 00:25:05.000
We had to match what we shot before because they weren't sure about the before, if they were going to see us before.
我们必须和之前拍的镜头衔接上，因为他们不确定之前的镜头，不确定是否会拍到我们之前的情况。

597
00:25:05.140 --> 00:25:06.640
So I had to match the clothes.
所以我必须穿同样的衣服。

598
00:25:06.720 --> 00:25:10.540
And I was wearing short sleeves and, like, a denim jumper.
我当时穿着短袖，还有一件牛仔背带裙。

599
00:25:11.340 --> 00:25:12.020
Yeah, yeah.
对，对。

600
00:25:12.180 --> 00:25:12.780
Like a kindergarten teacher.
就像个幼儿园老师一样。

601
00:25:12.960 --> 00:25:15.440
And I remember the Emmys were, like, the next week.
我记得艾美奖就在下一周。

602
00:25:15.520 --> 00:25:16.720
And I was so bruised.
我当时浑身都是淤青。

603
00:25:16.800 --> 00:25:17.840
I had to use, like, body makeup.
我不得不涂上那种身体粉底液。

604
00:25:18.020 --> 00:25:24.640
Yeah, because I think if they knew they were going to do the stunt that way, they probably would have padded you up and dressed you accordingly, right?
是啊，我觉得如果他们知道要那样做特技，大概会给你加护具，让你穿得更合适，对吧？

605
00:25:24.760 --> 00:25:25.204
Yes, totally.
没错，完全是这样。

606
00:25:25.204 --> 00:25:25.580
Yeah, yeah.
是啊，是啊。

607
00:25:25.680 --> 00:25:26.740
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

608
00:25:26.760 --> 00:25:27.480
That's crazy.
太疯狂了。

609
00:25:27.640 --> 00:25:30.340
Well, Kate, you did so many stunts on the show.
凯特，你在剧里做了那么多特技动作。

610
00:25:31.040 --> 00:25:32.120
Was this your favorite?
这是你最喜欢的一个吗？

611
00:25:32.280 --> 00:25:33.000
Do you even have a favorite?
你有最喜欢的吗？

612
00:25:33.000 --> 00:25:33.050
I think so.
我想是的。

613
00:25:33.100 --> 00:25:33.740
This was my favorite.
这就是我最喜欢的。

614
00:25:33.880 --> 00:25:35.480
I also loved being...
我也很喜欢……

615
00:25:35.480 --> 00:25:36.320
This is so weird.
这太奇怪了。

616
00:25:36.460 --> 00:25:40.280
I was on top of the men's room stall when Dwight comes.
德怀特进来的时候，我正趴在男厕所的隔间顶上。

617
00:25:40.280 --> 00:25:41.420
I was planking.
我在玩平板支撑。

618
00:25:41.640 --> 00:25:42.620
Meredith was planking.
梅雷迪思在玩平板支撑。

619
00:25:42.760 --> 00:25:43.060
Yes, yes.
对，对。

620
00:25:43.240 --> 00:25:48.820
Dwight comes in with a fire extinguisher and just blows her off into the stall.
德怀特拿着灭火器进来，直接把她喷进了隔间里。

621
00:25:49.800 --> 00:25:49.980
Yes.
没错。

622
00:25:50.440 --> 00:25:56.100
We used the real men's room, Video Village, where the guests were, those two bathrooMs.
我们用的是真正的男厕所，就在视频村，嘉宾们用的那两个洗手间。

623
00:25:56.100 --> 00:25:56.660
Yes, yeah.
对，是啊。

624
00:25:56.660 --> 00:25:57.200
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
是啊，是啊，是啊。

625
00:25:57.380 --> 00:26:01.760
And they put, like, this weird flim flam mattress on top.
他们在上面放了一个奇怪的简易床垫。

626
00:26:02.400 --> 00:26:06.580
And I was like, fingers crossed I don't go the other way because there was nothing on the other side.
我当时心想，祈祷我别掉到另一边去，因为那边什么都没有。

627
00:26:06.900 --> 00:26:07.960
Because I had to balance.
因为我得保持平衡。

628
00:26:08.260 --> 00:26:09.440
It was so crazy.
太疯狂了。

629
00:26:09.440 --> 00:26:10.300
But, yeah.
不过，确实。

630
00:26:10.460 --> 00:26:11.660
And it was really the men's room.
而且那真的是男厕所。

631
00:26:11.800 --> 00:26:15.680
I'm like, okay, hopefully I don't land too hard because then I'm going to hit the toilet.
我心想，好吧，希望我落地别太重，不然就要撞到马桶了。

632
00:26:15.860 --> 00:26:16.820
It's so bizarre.
真是太离谱了。

633
00:26:16.960 --> 00:26:17.720
But it was really fun.
但真的很有趣。

634
00:26:17.860 --> 00:26:20.760
I want to give some props to your athleticism.
我想夸夸你的运动天赋。

635
00:26:20.940 --> 00:26:26.540
I know that Angela has often chided me for my athleticism.
我知道安吉拉经常嘲笑我的运动能力。

636
00:26:26.760 --> 00:26:27.620
Here we go.
来了来了。

637
00:26:27.780 --> 00:26:28.940
No, it's okay.
不，没关系。

638
00:26:28.940 --> 00:26:32.500
I'm not going back to that anymore than I just did.
我不会再提刚才那茬了。

639
00:26:32.700 --> 00:26:37.380
But, Kate, you are amazingly athletic.
但是，凯特，你真的非常有运动天赋。

640
00:26:37.380 --> 00:26:40.100
I mean, in doing all these stunts, it doesn't surprise me.
我是说，做这些特技动作，我一点也不惊讶。

641
00:26:40.260 --> 00:26:43.660
I mean, we know that you were on Dancing with the Stars and you were amazing.
毕竟我们都知道你参加过《与星共舞》，表现得非常棒。

642
00:26:44.000 --> 00:26:48.000
But you also did your lounge show, The Lampshades, for years and years and years.
而且你还做了多年的酒廊表演《灯罩乐队》。

643
00:26:48.160 --> 00:26:50.100
And I remember coming to see you in that.
我记得我去看过你的演出。

644
00:26:50.100 --> 00:26:54.460
And you do this deep squat.
你做了一个深蹲动作。

645
00:26:55.940 --> 00:26:56.520
Repeatedly.
反复地做。

646
00:26:56.760 --> 00:26:57.520
Over and over again.
一次又一次。

647
00:26:57.780 --> 00:26:59.740
And you kick your leg up.
然后你把腿踢起来。

648
00:27:00.100 --> 00:27:02.700
And I was like, oh, my gosh.
我当时心想，天哪。

649
00:27:02.700 --> 00:27:09.580
I feel like they got so lucky with you as Meredith because you were qualified for these stunts.
我觉得他们选你演梅雷迪思真是太幸运了，因为你完全胜任这些特技动作。

650
00:27:09.660 --> 00:27:10.180
That's so sweet.
你真贴心。

651
00:27:10.180 --> 00:27:12.460
I feel like for me, too, it was empowering.
我觉得对我来说，这也是一种赋权。

652
00:27:12.640 --> 00:27:15.320
I did not do the stunt with my hair on fire.
我没有做那个头发着火的特技。

653
00:27:15.560 --> 00:27:18.200
I did do all the stuff in the parking lot of Moroccan Christmas.
但我确实拍了“摩洛哥圣诞”停车场里的所有戏份。

654
00:27:18.420 --> 00:27:19.700
I just didn't do the hair on fire.
只是没拍头发着火那段。

655
00:27:19.840 --> 00:27:20.720
You did the bat.
你拍了蝙蝠那场戏。

656
00:27:20.920 --> 00:27:21.760
That was crazy.
那太疯狂了。

657
00:27:21.760 --> 00:27:23.020
And you really sold it.
而且你演得特别逼真。

658
00:27:23.160 --> 00:27:23.840
So crazy.
太疯狂了。

659
00:27:23.980 --> 00:27:25.340
And then I didn't actually shave my head.
还有，我其实并没有剃光头。

660
00:27:25.380 --> 00:27:26.540
I had a bald cap for that.
我戴了个光头套。

661
00:27:26.660 --> 00:27:27.640
So I feel like those are the two.
所以我觉得就是这两件事。

662
00:27:27.720 --> 00:27:28.560
I'm like, okay.
我当时想，好吧。

663
00:27:28.860 --> 00:27:31.860
I think it's okay that you let your hair be.
我觉得你让头发保持原样也没关系。

664
00:27:32.080 --> 00:27:32.920
You know what I'm saying?
你明白我的意思吗？

665
00:27:32.940 --> 00:27:33.320
I know.
我明白。

666
00:27:33.380 --> 00:27:34.900
I think Greg was disappointed, though.
不过我觉得格雷格当时挺失望的。

667
00:27:35.040 --> 00:27:38.000
It was the first time I was like, nope, not doing that.
那是我第一次说，不，我不会那样做。

668
00:27:39.700 --> 00:27:44.260
Well, can we talk a little bit about the moment in this episode where we're all in the hospital?
那么，我们能聊聊这一集里大家都在医院的那场戏吗？

669
00:27:44.260 --> 00:27:45.840
We've all come to see you.
我们都来看你了。

670
00:27:46.720 --> 00:27:50.400
My memory of this was it was so hard to get through those scenes without laughing.
我记得拍那些戏的时候，要忍住不笑真的太难了。

671
00:27:50.560 --> 00:27:52.280
In fact, you see us break.
事实上，你们能看到我们笑场了。

672
00:27:52.380 --> 00:27:54.300
I fully break in the episode.
我在那一集里彻底笑场了。

673
00:27:54.520 --> 00:27:55.820
That was during Fun Run, yeah.
那是拍《欢乐跑》的时候，没错。

674
00:27:56.380 --> 00:27:58.560
What are your memories of shooting in the hospital?
你对在医院拍摄有什么记忆吗？

675
00:27:59.360 --> 00:28:04.240
I remember there was one scene where Dwight talks about the fact that if they pulled the plug,
我记得有一场戏，德怀特在说如果他们拔掉插头的话，

676
00:28:04.360 --> 00:28:05.420
basically the energy.
基本上就是能量的问题。

677
00:28:05.420 --> 00:28:08.140
Like they were wasting money, keeping you going.
就像他们是在浪费钱来维持你的生命一样。

678
00:28:08.300 --> 00:28:11.860
I loved it when you were like, do not pull the plug.
我特别喜欢你当时说，不要拔掉插头。

679
00:28:13.440 --> 00:28:15.000
Don't pull any plugs.
别拔掉任何插头。

680
00:28:15.160 --> 00:28:15.720
Oh, my God.
天哪。

681
00:28:15.840 --> 00:28:16.240
It's so good.
那段太棒了。

682
00:28:16.340 --> 00:28:19.040
And I remember the take when Steve just has an apology.
我还记得史蒂夫道歉的那次拍摄。

683
00:28:19.240 --> 00:28:21.000
He's trying to get an apology out of me, and I won't apologize.
他想让我道歉，但我就是不道歉。

684
00:28:21.000 --> 00:28:21.720
I won't apologize.
我绝不道歉。

685
00:28:21.960 --> 00:28:24.780
And so he just decides to climb into the bed with me.
于是他决定直接爬到我的病床上。

686
00:28:25.100 --> 00:28:28.700
And I feel like I had a slight delayed reaction, but I'm like, ah!
我感觉我的反应稍微迟钝了一点，但我当时想，啊！

687
00:28:28.920 --> 00:28:30.960
I just started screaming because I'm like, like.
我直接尖叫了起来，因为我当时觉得……

688
00:28:32.020 --> 00:28:36.940
Well, we were also surprised because he improvised that, and you even see all of us.
其实我们也吓了一跳，因为那是他即兴发挥的，你们甚至能看到我们所有人的反应。

689
00:28:37.040 --> 00:28:39.520
We sort of like freeze, and then we're like, Michael, stop!
我们当时都僵住了，然后喊道：迈克尔，住手！

690
00:28:39.740 --> 00:28:40.060
Yes!
没错！

691
00:28:40.340 --> 00:28:40.800
Yes!
没错！

692
00:28:42.020 --> 00:28:44.160
It really took us by surprise.
这真的让我们大吃一惊。

693
00:28:44.380 --> 00:28:44.680
Totally.
完全是。

694
00:28:45.140 --> 00:28:45.460
Totally.
完全是。

695
00:28:46.240 --> 00:28:52.000
Well, Kate, another question we like to ask our guests is if they took anything with them
那么，凯特，我们喜欢问嘉宾的另一个问题是，剧集杀青时你有没有带走什么东西？

696
00:28:52.000 --> 00:28:53.420
when the show wrapped.
剧集杀青时。

697
00:28:54.260 --> 00:28:55.360
How dare you?
你怎么敢这么问？

698
00:28:55.580 --> 00:28:55.820
I am not a thief.
我可不是小偷。

699
00:28:55.820 --> 00:28:56.920
Oh, what do you have it?
哦，你拿了什么？

700
00:28:56.920 --> 00:28:57.920
What do you have it for?
你拿它干什么？

701
00:28:57.920 --> 00:29:03.280
Well, first of all, I have Meredith's purse, which I always wore it like a, you know, like
首先，我有梅雷迪思的包，我总是把它背得像个，你知道，像

702
00:29:03.280 --> 00:29:03.760
a cross.
十字架一样。

703
00:29:04.000 --> 00:29:04.120
Like a side saddle.
像侧鞍一样。

704
00:29:04.560 --> 00:29:04.780
Yeah.
是啊。

705
00:29:05.260 --> 00:29:05.560
Yeah.
没错。

706
00:29:05.860 --> 00:29:07.120
You satcheled it.
你把它当挎包背了。

707
00:29:07.300 --> 00:29:09.700
And I left everything in it that was still in there.
我把里面剩下的所有东西都留着没动。

708
00:29:09.720 --> 00:29:16.240
So this is why I still had the marriage union of Pamela Morgan Beasley and James Duncan
所以这就是为什么我还有帕梅拉·摩根·比斯利和詹姆斯·邓肯

709
00:29:16.240 --> 00:29:16.700
Halpert.
·哈尔珀特的结婚证书。

710
00:29:17.160 --> 00:29:18.540
Is that our wedding?
那是我们的婚礼吗？

711
00:29:18.560 --> 00:29:19.760
Yes, it's the program.
是的，那是流程单。

712
00:29:19.980 --> 00:29:20.720
So this is what I did.
所以我当时就是这么做的。

713
00:29:20.720 --> 00:29:21.540
It's our wedding program.
那是我们的婚礼流程单。

714
00:29:21.540 --> 00:29:22.140
The wedding party.
婚礼派对。

715
00:29:22.280 --> 00:29:22.900
And the wedding party.
还有婚礼派对。

716
00:29:22.900 --> 00:29:28.880
Yes, this is what I showed on Some Good News with John Krasinski when we did our wedding
没错，这就是我在约翰·卡拉辛斯基的《好消息》节目里展示的东西，当时我们做了婚礼

717
00:29:28.880 --> 00:29:29.160
gifts.
礼物。

718
00:29:29.180 --> 00:29:30.020
Oh my gosh.
天哪。

719
00:29:30.120 --> 00:29:30.640
Isn't that crazy?
这不疯狂吗？

720
00:29:31.320 --> 00:29:34.700
That is so, that you had just tucked it in your purse and you still have it.
太不可思议了，你竟然把它塞在包里，而且还一直留着。

721
00:29:34.700 --> 00:29:34.860
I did.
我确实留着。

722
00:29:34.960 --> 00:29:36.060
We would do that though.
不过我们确实会那样做。

723
00:29:36.240 --> 00:29:40.520
We would get prop purses and like if we had props, we would just put them in our purse.
我们会拿道具包，如果手头有道具，我们就会直接塞进包里。

724
00:29:40.760 --> 00:29:40.810
Totally.
完全同意。

725
00:29:40.980 --> 00:29:41.200
Yeah.
是啊。

726
00:29:41.380 --> 00:29:43.160
I have, oh my gosh, what else do I have in here?
我还有，天哪，我这里面还有什么？

727
00:29:43.320 --> 00:29:44.320
I think I have.
我想我有。

728
00:29:44.640 --> 00:29:45.740
Do you have some old sides?
你有旧的剧本页吗？

729
00:29:45.900 --> 00:29:47.460
I would always put my sides in my purse.
我总是把剧本页放在包里。

730
00:29:47.460 --> 00:29:47.510
I do have sides.
我确实有剧本页。

731
00:29:47.510 --> 00:29:47.560
Yes, I do have sides.
是的，我确实有。

732
00:29:47.660 --> 00:29:51.660
But I also have, I have Sweeney Todd from when Andy was performing in that theater.
但我还有，我有安迪在剧院表演时的《理发师陶德》剧本。

733
00:29:51.920 --> 00:29:52.240
Wow.
哇。

734
00:29:53.360 --> 00:30:00.860
We have Church of Angels, Cecilia Marie Halpert when she got christened, Cece's christened.
我们还有天使教堂，塞西莉亚·玛丽·哈尔珀特受洗时的东西，西西受洗了。

735
00:30:01.220 --> 00:30:03.020
Oh my gosh, Kate.
天哪，凯特。

736
00:30:03.220 --> 00:30:04.260
These are amazing.
这些太棒了。

737
00:30:04.400 --> 00:30:04.800
I know.
我知道。

738
00:30:04.800 --> 00:30:08.920
Well, Kate, fans love Meredith and you know we're going to be hitting you up.
好吧，凯特，粉丝们很爱梅雷迪思，你知道我们会再来找你的。

739
00:30:09.180 --> 00:30:13.440
We've got a few more episodes to cover before we're done here.
在结束之前，我们还有几集要讲。

740
00:30:13.820 --> 00:30:17.280
Before we say goodbye, is there anything we can share with everyone?
在告别之前，有什么我们可以和大家分享的吗？

741
00:30:17.600 --> 00:30:18.380
Like where to find you?
比如在哪里可以找到你？

742
00:30:18.460 --> 00:30:19.220
What you're up to?
你最近在忙什么？

743
00:30:19.900 --> 00:30:26.620
Yes, I, well on Instagram at TheRealKateFlannery, on Twitter at Kate Flannery.
有的，我在Instagram上是TheRealKateFlannery，在Twitter上是Kate Flannery。

744
00:30:26.800 --> 00:30:29.900
I go to a little ramen place once a week in K-10.
我每周去K-10的一家小拉面店一次。

745
00:30:29.900 --> 00:30:30.520
Don't say that.
别说那个。

746
00:30:31.760 --> 00:30:38.080
But I'm actually doing some charity work for Phil Abundance, which is the biggest food bank
但我实际上在为Phil Abundance做一些慈善工作，那是费城最大的

747
00:30:38.080 --> 00:30:38.660
in Philadelphia.
食品银行。

748
00:30:38.860 --> 00:30:39.820
That's my hometown.
那是我的家乡。

749
00:30:40.340 --> 00:30:44.100
I'm working with WMMR, which is the big radio station.
我正在和WMMR合作，那是当地的大型广播电台。

750
00:30:44.280 --> 00:30:46.940
They always have the big morning show with Preston and Steve.
他们一直有普雷斯顿和史蒂夫主持的大型早间节目。

751
00:30:47.060 --> 00:30:48.260
And I've been doing their show for years.
我做他们的节目已经好多年了。

752
00:30:48.580 --> 00:30:51.180
And it's literally like five minutes from my dad's house.
而且离我爸家真的只有五分钟路程。

753
00:30:51.300 --> 00:30:52.400
Like I will roll out of bed.
我简直可以从床上滚过去。

754
00:30:52.480 --> 00:30:57.400
And if I'm in town, I just, and I occasionally sometimes let a four-letter word slip.
如果我在城里，我偶尔会不小心说漏嘴，蹦出个脏字来。

755
00:30:57.520 --> 00:31:01.580
So they literally have a button on their panel that says the Flannery button.
所以他们的控制台上真的有一个按钮，上面写着“弗兰纳里按钮”。

756
00:31:01.580 --> 00:31:03.400
Because it was a four-second, you know, five-second rule.
因为那有个四秒，你知道的，五秒规则。

757
00:31:03.580 --> 00:31:04.400
Like, oh, they had, oh, whatever.
就像，噢，他们有，噢，随便吧。

758
00:31:05.280 --> 00:31:06.840
Those FCCs, gosh, it's crazy.
那些联邦通信委员会的规定，天哪，真是疯了。

759
00:31:06.940 --> 00:31:09.360
But anyway, I love these guys so much.
但不管怎样，我太爱这帮家伙了。

760
00:31:09.420 --> 00:31:10.680
And they're making such a difference.
他们真的做出了很大的贡献。

761
00:31:10.880 --> 00:31:13.320
Phil Abundance is, they're doing a huge push.
Phil Abundance正在进行大规模的推广活动。

762
00:31:13.400 --> 00:31:14.720
They always do it right before Thanksgiving.
他们总是在感恩节前夕做这件事。

763
00:31:15.180 --> 00:31:18.380
But in the meantime, you know, you guys can go to philabundance.org.
但在此期间，你们可以去philabundance.org看看。

764
00:31:18.980 --> 00:31:22.040
And I'm going to be doing some, a little bit of press for them.
我也会为他们做一些宣传工作。

765
00:31:22.200 --> 00:31:23.920
And I'll be, you know.
我会，你知道的。

766
00:31:23.940 --> 00:31:25.300
Kate, that is so great.
凯特，那真是太棒了。

767
00:31:25.300 --> 00:31:28.680
And we should have mentioned that you are from Pennsylvania.
我们应该提一下你是宾夕法尼亚州人。

768
00:31:29.000 --> 00:31:29.260
Yes.
是的。

769
00:31:29.260 --> 00:31:32.900
And that your family, your dad had a bar in Philly.
而且你的家人，你爸爸在费城开过一家酒吧。

770
00:31:33.080 --> 00:31:34.180
What was the name of the bar?
那家酒吧叫什么名字？

771
00:31:34.400 --> 00:31:35.120
Lannery's Tavern.
兰纳里酒馆。

772
00:31:35.340 --> 00:31:37.220
He was up all night trying to figure out a name.
他整晚没睡都在想名字。

773
00:31:37.360 --> 00:31:37.720
No, I'm just kidding.
不，我开玩笑的。

774
00:31:38.320 --> 00:31:39.760
My grandfather came up with a name.
是我祖父想的名字。

775
00:31:40.680 --> 00:31:45.040
Well, Kate, we love that you are giving back to Philly like that.
好吧，凯特，我们很喜欢你这样回馈费城。

776
00:31:45.160 --> 00:31:49.200
And we'll definitely, you know, we'll put in our socials where people can find that.
我们一定会把相关信息发到社交媒体上，让大家知道去哪里参与。

777
00:31:49.200 --> 00:31:49.840
That would be awesome.
那太棒了。

778
00:31:50.060 --> 00:31:50.760
Thank you so much.
非常感谢。

779
00:31:50.820 --> 00:31:51.980
You guys, I love you.
你们好，我爱你们。

780
00:31:52.200 --> 00:31:53.080
So great to see you.
很高兴见到你们。

781
00:31:53.240 --> 00:31:53.320
Love you too.
我们也爱你。

782
00:31:53.500 --> 00:31:54.620
Thank you so much, Kate.
非常感谢你，凯特。

783
00:31:54.660 --> 00:31:55.460
This was amazing.
这太棒了。

784
00:31:55.460 --> 00:31:56.560
You have to come back.
你一定要再来。

785
00:31:56.820 --> 00:31:57.560
I would love to.
我很乐意。

786
00:32:06.220 --> 00:32:07.900
Oh, we are back.
噢，我们回来了。

787
00:32:08.060 --> 00:32:11.420
Angela, that was so great talking with Kate.
安吉拉，和凯特聊天真是太棒了。

788
00:32:11.640 --> 00:32:13.660
She looks beautiful, stunning.
她看起来很美，惊艳极了。

789
00:32:13.920 --> 00:32:18.720
We have been talking to a lot of people through Zoom for our podcaSt.
我们通过Zoom和很多人聊过我们的播客。

790
00:32:18.720 --> 00:32:22.100
And most people show up like a hot mess.
大多数人出现时都邋里邋遢的。

791
00:32:22.300 --> 00:32:23.560
Not Kate Flannery.
凯特·弗兰纳里可不是。

