01:01:28.260 --> 01:01:46.500
All right, we are back, and Angela, Michael has gone into the break room in an attempt to rally everyone to plant a tree in honor of Meredith.
好了，我们回来了。安吉拉，迈克尔已经进了休息室，试图召集大家种一棵树来纪念梅雷迪思。

1420
01:01:47.300 --> 01:01:49.400
But do you know what I titled this scene?
但你知道我给这场戏起了什么标题吗？

1421
01:01:49.520 --> 01:01:52.840
You are always titling scenes, and I have titled a scene.
你总是给场景起标题，我也给一个场景起过标题。

1422
01:01:53.040 --> 01:01:53.160
What?
什么？

1423
01:01:54.520 --> 01:01:55.960
John eats popcorn.
约翰吃爆米花。

1424
01:01:56.580 --> 01:01:57.780
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1425
01:01:58.580 --> 01:02:02.840
Did you notice he is eating popcorn through this whole scene?
你注意到他整场戏都在吃爆米花吗？

1426
01:02:03.020 --> 01:02:05.560
Not carrots, not baby carrots, but popcorn.
不是胡萝卜，不是小胡萝卜，而是爆米花。

1427
01:02:05.700 --> 01:02:11.400
And the way he's eating it, it's so, it's so delicate.
而且他吃的方式，太，太优雅了。

1428
01:02:12.060 --> 01:02:14.560
Was he trying not to crunch too loudly?
他是想尽量不发出太大的咀嚼声吗？

1429
01:02:14.920 --> 01:02:21.900
I think he was trying not to be a problem for sound, but he was clearly hungry because he eats it through the whole scene.
我想他是尽量不想给收音造成麻烦，但他显然饿了，因为他整场戏都在吃。

1430
01:02:21.900 --> 01:02:22.980
Oh, my God.
天哪。

1431
01:02:23.120 --> 01:02:26.960
Was this the year we got that little popcorn maker by Kraft Services?
这是我们从卡夫服务公司拿到那个小爆米花机的那一年吗？

1432
01:02:28.160 --> 01:02:29.280
It must have been.
一定是那年。

1433
01:02:29.420 --> 01:02:32.240
This must have been the first week with the popcorn maker.
这一定是有了爆米花机的第一周。

1434
01:02:32.240 --> 01:02:37.160
We went a little crazy for popcorn, and then the sound department, I think, said, okay, guys.
我们对爆米花有点疯狂，然后录音部门，我想，他们说，好了，伙计们。

1435
01:02:37.740 --> 01:02:39.220
I remember it went away.
我记得后来它就消失了。

1436
01:02:39.440 --> 01:02:41.520
Yeah, but we were excited about it.
是啊，但我们当时很兴奋。

1437
01:02:41.720 --> 01:02:49.360
Well, he's eating popcorn in this whole scene, and it's also in this scene that Pam explains to Michael, you know, we're just going to go visit Meredith.
好吧，他整场戏都在吃爆米花，而且也是在这场戏里，帕姆向迈克尔解释说，你知道，我们只是去探望梅雷迪思。

1438
01:02:49.360 --> 01:02:52.100
We're going to go in shifts so we don't overwhelm her.
我们会分批去，这样就不会让她应接不暇。

1439
01:02:52.260 --> 01:02:55.260
But Michael is like, no, we're all going together.
但迈克尔说，不，我们要一起去。

1440
01:02:55.260 --> 01:02:57.160
At the same time, I'll drive.
同时去，我来开车。

1441
01:02:57.160 --> 01:03:06.080
So Jim and Pam are like, well, we can each take people in our separate cars, and Oscar's like, separate cars, and Kevin's like, I don't believe it.
所以吉姆和帕姆说，好吧，我们可以各自开车带人，奥斯卡说，分开开车，凯文说，我不信。

1442
01:03:06.420 --> 01:03:07.020
I know.
我知道。

1443
01:03:07.320 --> 01:03:12.740
Well, then Michael has a talking head, and he says, you know, I have flaws, you know, so sue me.
然后迈克尔有个采访镜头，他说，你知道，我有缺点，你知道，去告我吧。

1444
01:03:12.800 --> 01:03:14.100
And he's like, no, no, no, don't sue me.
然后他说，不，不，不，别告我。

1445
01:03:14.420 --> 01:03:25.360
But Jenna, there was an alt to this talking head, and it's in the deleted scenes, and it made me laugh so hard, and it's also in the bloopers, and Steve couldn't get through it.
但是珍娜，这个采访镜头有个备选版本，在删减片段里，我当时笑得不行，而且花絮里也有，史蒂夫一直演不下去。

1446
01:03:25.360 --> 01:03:26.100
He kept laughing.
他一直在笑。

1447
01:03:26.800 --> 01:03:27.700
What is it?
是什么？

1448
01:03:27.740 --> 01:03:28.120
Okay.
好吧。

1449
01:03:28.520 --> 01:03:29.880
This is it.
就是这个。

1450
01:03:29.980 --> 01:03:30.680
There's one take.
有一个镜头。

1451
01:03:30.860 --> 01:03:33.180
Clearly, he got through it, because it's in the deleted scenes.
很显然，他挺过来了，因为这在删减片段里。

1452
01:03:33.660 --> 01:03:36.520
He says, I am not a bad guy.
他说，我不是个坏人。

1453
01:03:36.960 --> 01:03:40.200
I am a good guy who runs over women with his car.
我是个好人，只是开车撞了女人而已。

1454
01:03:41.320 --> 01:03:44.340
Why am I having such a hard time getting my message across?
为什么我这么难把我的意思表达清楚呢？

1455
01:03:45.400 --> 01:03:46.520
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1456
01:03:46.540 --> 01:03:47.340
That is funny.
那太搞笑了。

1457
01:03:47.860 --> 01:03:50.560
And the way Steve does it is so good.
而且史蒂夫演得太棒了。

1458
01:03:50.880 --> 01:03:51.660
That's good.
那很好。

1459
01:03:51.660 --> 01:03:52.960
I have to go watch that.
我得去看看那个。

1460
01:03:53.020 --> 01:03:53.700
Yeah, you have to.
是啊，你一定要看。

1461
01:03:53.700 --> 01:04:00.600
Well, we don't find out exactly how they get there, but the entire gang does arrive at the hospital.
我们没看到他们具体是怎么去的，但整群人都到了医院。

1462
01:04:00.880 --> 01:04:03.300
Michael has a whole bunch of balloons.
迈克尔带了一大堆气球。

1463
01:04:03.460 --> 01:04:05.420
And the entire gang minus Dwight.
除了德怀特，全员到齐。

1464
01:04:06.360 --> 01:04:10.380
That's right, because Dwight has gone to take care of Sprinkles.
没错，因为德怀特去处理“洒洒”的事了。

1465
01:04:10.540 --> 01:04:10.840
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1466
01:04:11.740 --> 01:04:21.620
Everyone gathers around Meredith's bed, and we talked about this scene with Kate, about how Steve improvised crawling on top of her in that one moment.
大家围在梅雷迪思的病床边，我们和凯特聊过这一幕，聊到史蒂夫当时即兴爬到她身上的那一刻。

1467
01:04:21.620 --> 01:04:23.660
He's, like, trying to give her a hug.
他就像是想给她一个拥抱。

1468
01:04:23.960 --> 01:04:25.140
It's pretty amazing.
真是太神奇了。

1469
01:04:25.440 --> 01:04:25.920
It's pretty great.
太棒了。

1470
01:04:25.920 --> 01:04:35.520
There is a deleted scene from this moment where Creed, as they're exiting, just grabs all her meds out of the little plastic cups they're sitting on her tray.
这一幕有个删减片段，克里德在他们离开时，直接把她托盘上塑料杯里的药全抓走了。

1471
01:04:35.840 --> 01:04:36.360
Oh.
哦。

1472
01:04:36.520 --> 01:04:38.460
And Creed just pockets all her meds.
克里德就把她的药全揣兜里了。

1473
01:04:39.560 --> 01:04:40.780
Of course he does.
他当然会这么做。

1474
01:04:41.480 --> 01:04:47.640
Well, I had a favorite moment from this scene, and I wanted to ask you about it because I think maybe you improvised it.
这一幕里我有个最喜欢的瞬间，我想问问你，因为我觉得那可能是你即兴发挥的。

1475
01:04:47.800 --> 01:04:59.680
When Michael is trying to get Meredith to forgive him, he says that she should think about the Bible because it says that forgiveness is next to godliness.
当迈克尔试图让梅雷迪思原谅他时，他说她应该想想《圣经》，因为上面说宽恕仅次于神圣。

1476
01:04:59.880 --> 01:05:00.200
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1477
01:05:00.200 --> 01:05:03.280
And you mutter, that's cleanliness.
然后你嘟囔了一句，那是整洁。

1478
01:05:03.660 --> 01:05:04.780
I did improvise that.
那确实是我即兴说的。

1479
01:05:06.600 --> 01:05:13.060
Oh, I also wanted to mention in this scene the nurse, who is an improv person from IO.
哦，我还想提一下这一幕里的护士，她是来自IO的即兴表演者。

1480
01:05:13.060 --> 01:05:14.880
Her name is Sylvia McClure.
她叫西尔维娅·麦克卢尔。

1481
01:05:15.740 --> 01:05:19.040
Well, I looked at her IMDb, and I found this very interesting.
我查了她的IMDb，发现了一件很有趣的事。

1482
01:05:19.620 --> 01:05:27.420
In addition to playing a nurse on The Office, she has also played a doctor on Young and the Restless, Dexter, and Intelligence.
除了在《办公室》里演护士，她还在《不安分的青春》、《嗜血法医》和《智能缉凶》里演过医生。

1483
01:05:27.420 --> 01:05:32.320
A nurse in Night of the Dead, and a receptionist nurse on the unit.
在《死亡之夜》里演过护士，还在某个单元里演过接待护士。

1484
01:05:33.460 --> 01:05:39.460
So she's played a lot of nurses and doctors, and incidentally, she's also twice been cast as a nun.
所以她演过很多护士和医生，顺便一提，她还两次被选角演修女。

1485
01:05:40.240 --> 01:05:41.880
That is very interesting.
那太有趣了。

1486
01:05:42.340 --> 01:05:45.420
Like, sort of a, it's like a weird typecasting.
就像是一种奇怪的定型化选角。

1487
01:05:46.220 --> 01:05:46.760
Yeah.
是啊。

1488
01:05:47.340 --> 01:05:47.880
Exactly.
没错。

1489
01:05:48.180 --> 01:05:52.960
Well, I used to get a lot of auditions for schoolteachers and nurses.
我以前也经常接到试镜，演学校老师和护士。

1490
01:05:53.320 --> 01:05:55.320
Have you ever played a nurse or doctor?
你演过护士或医生吗？

1491
01:05:56.000 --> 01:05:57.180
Yes, actually.
有，其实演过。

1492
01:05:57.420 --> 01:06:02.580
I played a pediatric nurse in this movie called The Promotion.
我在一部叫《晋升》的电影里演过儿科护士。

1493
01:06:03.080 --> 01:06:07.740
I played a doctor on an episode of Monk.
我在《神探阿蒙》的一集里演过医生。

1494
01:06:08.340 --> 01:06:09.100
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1495
01:06:09.240 --> 01:06:15.280
And I played a sexy nurse briefly in one of our Halloween episodes of The Office.
而且我在《办公室》的一集万圣节特辑里短暂地演过性感护士。

1496
01:06:16.380 --> 01:06:20.340
What were you most often typecast as for auditions?
你试镜时最常被定型为什么角色？

1497
01:06:21.100 --> 01:06:22.640
Before The Office?
在《办公室》之前吗？

1498
01:06:22.920 --> 01:06:24.360
Before The Office.
在《办公室》之前。

1499
01:06:24.760 --> 01:06:25.460
Quirky.
古怪的。

1500
01:06:25.660 --> 01:06:26.540
Quirky gal.
古怪的女孩。

1501
01:06:26.540 --> 01:06:27.440
Well, what's up?
好吧，怎么了？

1502
01:06:27.500 --> 01:06:29.180
Like, quirky, fun neighbor.
就像那种古怪、有趣的邻居。

1503
01:06:29.440 --> 01:06:29.980
Quirky neighbor.
古怪的邻居。

1504
01:06:30.780 --> 01:06:31.180
Yeah.
是啊。

1505
01:06:31.280 --> 01:06:32.080
Ba-da-da-da-do-do.
吧嗒嗒嗒嘟嘟。

1506
01:06:33.120 --> 01:06:33.520
Yeah.
是啊。

1507
01:06:33.880 --> 01:06:39.980
I was, I got a lot of just the schoolteachers, waitresses, and nurses.
我当时，我接到的角色大多是学校老师、服务员和护士。

1508
01:06:40.280 --> 01:06:40.480
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1509
01:06:41.080 --> 01:06:45.700
Well, I will tell you, we talked about how hard we laughed in this scene, but 11 minutes,
我跟你说，我们聊过这场戏我们笑得有多厉害，但在11分

1510
01:06:45.840 --> 01:06:47.900
22 seconds is when you can see us breaking.
22秒的时候，你能看到我们笑场了。

1511
01:06:47.900 --> 01:06:52.340
If you're looking for it, that's when Michael crawls on top of Meredith.
如果你仔细看，那就是迈克尔爬到梅雷迪思身上的时候。

1512
01:06:52.960 --> 01:07:00.940
Well, now we can go back to The Office, and we are going to find Dwight telling Angela
好了，现在回到《办公室》，我们要看看德怀特告诉安吉拉

1513
01:07:00.940 --> 01:07:02.120
some bad news.
一个坏消息。

1514
01:07:02.120 --> 01:07:03.720
And she's anxious to see him.
她很急切地想见到他。

1515
01:07:03.860 --> 01:07:05.360
She wants to know how it went.
她想知道结果如何。

1516
01:07:05.500 --> 01:07:06.420
You can just tell.
一眼就能看出来。

1517
01:07:06.860 --> 01:07:07.260
Yeah.
是啊。

1518
01:07:07.260 --> 01:07:08.360
And then he's like, hey, monkey.
然后他说，嘿，小猴子。

1519
01:07:08.520 --> 01:07:09.540
And she's like, any problems?
她说，有什么问题吗？

1520
01:07:09.980 --> 01:07:12.520
Well, you left the TV on, and your cat is dead.
好吧，你电视没关，而且你的猫死了。

1521
01:07:13.160 --> 01:07:15.480
And my character's like, what?
我的角色当时就想，什么？

1522
01:07:15.880 --> 01:07:18.720
And he's like, Sparkles, the white one, is dead.
他说，斯帕克尔斯，那只白色的猫，死了。

1523
01:07:18.720 --> 01:07:20.600
Yeah, he gets the name wrong.
是啊，他名字还叫错了。

1524
01:07:20.820 --> 01:07:21.460
It's bad.
太糟糕了。

1525
01:07:21.580 --> 01:07:22.280
It is bad.
确实很糟糕。

1526
01:07:22.560 --> 01:07:24.020
This will not end well.
这事儿没法善终。

1527
01:07:24.740 --> 01:07:30.980
Angela, you get so very immediately emotional, and not in a funny way.
安吉拉，你立刻就变得非常情绪化，而且不是那种搞笑的方式。

1528
01:07:31.140 --> 01:07:38.260
Like, this is one of the ways that our show allowed characters to be real people, because
这是我们剧集让角色变得真实的方式之一，因为

1529
01:07:39.300 --> 01:07:44.400
Angela, the character, really loved her cat, and she is heartbroken.
安吉拉这个角色真的很爱她的猫，她心碎了。

1530
01:07:44.760 --> 01:07:48.060
And you see that real pain here from your character.
你在这里看到了你角色真实的痛苦。

1531
01:07:48.060 --> 01:07:50.360
How did you gear up for this scene?
你是怎么为这场戏做准备的？

1532
01:07:51.080 --> 01:07:57.140
Well, Greg told me, he said, you know, Angela Martin, hearing this news will be devastated.
格雷格告诉我，他说，你知道，安吉拉·马丁听到这个消息会崩溃的。

1533
01:07:57.740 --> 01:08:05.320
And I need you to play out the beats of hearing news that kind of destroys you in the moment.
我需要你表现出听到那种瞬间摧毁你的消息时的心路历程。

1534
01:08:05.480 --> 01:08:10.260
You know, and I feel like we've all had moments in our lives where we've gotten that phone call
你知道，我觉得我们生活中都有过那种时刻，就是接到电话

1535
01:08:10.260 --> 01:08:12.500
with some bad news, you know, unfortunately.
听到坏消息的时候，很不幸。

1536
01:08:12.500 --> 01:08:20.340
Unfortunately, and I just sort of thought about a few of those moments where, you know, at first,
不幸的是，我当时就想到了那几个时刻，你知道，起初，

1537
01:08:20.500 --> 01:08:24.400
you're just in total shock where you're not really sure what you heard.
你完全处于震惊中，甚至不确定自己听到了什么。

1538
01:08:25.220 --> 01:08:25.660
Yeah.
是啊。

1539
01:08:25.820 --> 01:08:29.400
And then it's like someone slaps you in the face with the information.
然后就像有人当面给了你一记耳光，让你清醒地意识到这个消息。

1540
01:08:30.660 --> 01:08:33.980
And then you're trying to make sense of it, but you can't make sense of it.
接着你试图理清头绪，但根本理不清。

1541
01:08:34.580 --> 01:08:35.840
It's the unthinkable.
那是不可思议的事。

1542
01:08:35.980 --> 01:08:37.440
And it doesn't make sense.
而且完全说不通。

1543
01:08:37.740 --> 01:08:39.680
And your body is doing all of that.
你的身体正在经历这一切。

1544
01:08:39.960 --> 01:08:40.820
You're in shock.
你处于震惊中。

1545
01:08:40.980 --> 01:08:41.800
You're sad.
你很悲伤。

1546
01:08:42.280 --> 01:08:46.160
Your body, your mind is trying to make it right, but you can't make it right.
你的身体、你的大脑试图去修正它，但你无法修正。

1547
01:08:46.340 --> 01:08:47.420
You can't figure it out.
你无法弄明白。

1548
01:08:47.560 --> 01:08:49.040
You don't understand why it happened.
你不明白为什么会发生这种事。

1549
01:08:49.040 --> 01:08:53.000
And I was just trying to process through all of that.
我当时只是试图去消化所有这些情绪。

1550
01:08:53.440 --> 01:08:56.360
And yeah, that's what I did.
是的，我就是这么做的。

1551
01:08:56.540 --> 01:08:58.700
Did you have to do a lot of takes of that scene?
那场戏你拍了很多遍吗？

1552
01:08:58.700 --> 01:08:59.340
Do you remember?
你还记得吗？

1553
01:08:59.660 --> 01:09:00.580
No, I didn't.
不，没有。

1554
01:09:00.640 --> 01:09:01.920
I was thankful for that.
对此我很庆幸。

1555
01:09:02.240 --> 01:09:05.060
In the next scene, your character is still crying.
在下一场戏里，你的角色还在哭。

1556
01:09:05.260 --> 01:09:11.460
She's standing at reception with Pam, and you look like you've been crying for a long time.
她和帕姆站在接待处，看起来你已经哭了很久了。

1557
01:09:11.900 --> 01:09:17.200
What did you do to get there, to start the scene in a place like that?
你是怎么做到的，让自己在开拍时就进入那种状态？

1558
01:09:17.200 --> 01:09:21.660
You know, I'm chatty, so my instinct would be, I'm standing by reception with you, would
你知道，我这人爱聊天，所以我的本能反应是，既然和你一起站在接待处，

1559
01:09:21.660 --> 01:09:24.780
be to be hanging out, you know, being part of the bullpen.
就会想闲聊，你知道，融入大家。

1560
01:09:25.020 --> 01:09:29.780
So one of the things I did was I went around the corner by the elevators, by myself, in
所以我采取的方法之一是，在拍摄间隙，

1561
