他在说出“豪猪的身体”之前，停顿了那么久？

1705
01:17:18.360 --> 01:17:18.960
Yes.
没错。

1706
01:17:19.180 --> 01:17:20.060
We were on the floor.
我们当时都笑瘫在地上了。

1707
01:17:20.240 --> 01:17:21.620
We were on the floor.
我们都笑得倒在地上。

1708
01:17:21.800 --> 01:17:27.420
I am not in any background shots while he's doing these animal combinations because I couldn't keep it together.
当他表演这些动物组合时，我根本没法出现在背景镜头里，因为我实在憋不住笑。

1709
01:17:27.980 --> 01:17:33.680
And at 18 minutes, 11 seconds, you can see Craig Robinson covering his face.
在18分11秒的时候，你可以看到克雷格·罗宾逊捂住了脸。

1710
01:17:33.980 --> 01:17:35.100
I saw it.
我看到了。

1711
01:17:35.380 --> 01:17:36.660
I remember that.
我记得那一幕。

1712
01:17:36.660 --> 01:17:39.280
But we were losing it.
但我们当时真的快失控了。

1713
01:17:39.960 --> 01:17:42.600
It was so funny.
太好笑了。

1714
01:17:42.820 --> 01:17:45.380
And they let him go for a long time.
而且他们让他演了很久。

1715
01:17:45.900 --> 01:17:48.160
I mean, you are not seeing all of it.
我是说，你们看到的并不是全部。

1716
01:17:48.260 --> 01:17:50.040
He went for so long.
他演了很长时间。

1717
01:17:50.220 --> 01:17:55.840
And I remember we were cracking up and we were just like, as a group, we were like, no, get it together.
我记得我们当时笑得不行，大家都在互相提醒，不行，得稳住。

1718
01:17:56.000 --> 01:17:56.840
These are too good.
这些段子太棒了。

1719
01:17:56.940 --> 01:17:57.880
We can't ruin these.
我们不能把这些镜头毁了。

1720
01:17:58.540 --> 01:18:03.900
Well, while all this is happening at the office, Dwight has gone to visit Meredith.
好吧，当办公室里发生这一切的时候，德怀特去探望梅雷迪思了。

1721
01:18:04.500 --> 01:18:16.280
Meredith, and he has this talking head where he's saying, as he's sitting next to her, that sometimes the best thing to do is to put an animal out of its misery.
梅雷迪思，他坐在她身边时有一段独白，说有时候最好的做法就是让动物安乐死。

1722
01:18:16.640 --> 01:18:17.480
He's a farmer.
他是个农夫嘛。

1723
01:18:17.780 --> 01:18:18.120
Yeah.
是啊。

1724
01:18:18.480 --> 01:18:23.480
You could power a small fan for two days with the amount of electricity Meredith is hooked up to.
梅雷迪思身上连着的那些医疗设备耗电量，足以让一个小风扇转上两天。

1725
01:18:24.200 --> 01:18:38.500
I have to say, please, if you go back to rewatch this episode, during this speech by Dwight next to Meredith's bedside, please look at the woman in the bed on the other side.
我得说，拜托，如果你回头重看这一集，在德怀特于梅雷迪思床边发表这段演说时，请留意一下另一边床上的那位女士。

1726
01:18:39.320 --> 01:18:39.920
Okay?
好吗？

1727
01:18:40.320 --> 01:18:41.760
Over Dwight's shoulder.
就在德怀特的肩膀后面。

1728
01:18:42.680 --> 01:18:43.800
That's all I'm going to say.
我只能说这么多了。

1729
01:18:43.920 --> 01:18:46.940
Just enjoy that performance the next time you watch this scene.
下次看这一幕时，好好欣赏她的表演吧。

1730
01:18:47.520 --> 01:18:48.580
It's wonderful.
太精彩了。

1731
01:18:48.580 --> 01:18:50.040
Oh, my God, Jenna.
天哪，珍娜。

1732
01:18:50.400 --> 01:18:53.720
When we were all crammed around Kate's bed, that woman was there.
当我们都挤在凯特的床边时，那位女士就在那儿。

1733
01:18:55.060 --> 01:19:00.200
I swear, that woman, it was like she was a real patient.
我发誓，那位女士，她看起来就像个真正的病人。

1734
01:19:01.180 --> 01:19:06.060
She let out some kind of noise, and I thought we were all going to shit our pants.
她发出了一种声音，我以为我们当时都要吓尿了。

1735
01:19:07.040 --> 01:19:12.480
She was a background actor, but she was so real.
她是个背景演员，但她演得太真实了。

1736
01:19:12.480 --> 01:19:21.000
Well, she literally, while we were standing there one time, went, like, I think they told her to maybe make a moaning sound.
有一次我们站在那儿的时候，她真的，我想他们可能让她发出一点呻吟声。

1737
01:19:21.260 --> 01:19:21.540
Yeah.
是的。

1738
01:19:21.660 --> 01:19:24.860
And her interpretation of that, we went loopy.
而她对这个要求的演绎，让我们彻底疯了。

1739
01:19:25.300 --> 01:19:28.500
Well, watch her in the background of the scene because she's excellent.
总之，留意一下背景里的她，因为她演得太棒了。

1740
01:19:28.780 --> 01:19:32.180
So now the doctor comes in, and Dwight has some questions for him.
现在医生进来了，德怀特有一些问题要问他。

1741
01:19:32.500 --> 01:19:36.500
And you and I both know that this is our writer, Justin Spitzer.
你我都清楚，这位医生就是我们的编剧贾斯汀·斯皮策。

1742
01:19:38.080 --> 01:19:42.500
Yes, creator of some of your favorite Dwightisms, Justin Spitzer.
没错，就是创作了你最喜欢的那些“德怀特语录”的贾斯汀·斯皮策。

1743
01:19:42.780 --> 01:19:44.900
And the creator of the show, Superstore.
也是《爆笑超市》的创作者。

1744
01:19:45.300 --> 01:19:50.500
Well, I reached out to Justin, and he told me that he got this role after reading the part in the table read.
我联系了贾斯汀，他告诉我，他在剧本围读会上读了这个角色后，就得到了这个机会。

1745
01:19:51.480 --> 01:19:53.040
That he made Greg laugh.
因为他把格雷格逗笑了。

1746
01:19:53.180 --> 01:19:55.400
Which Paul Lieberstein has shared that this would happen.
保罗·利伯斯坦曾分享过，这种情况时有发生。

1747
01:19:55.400 --> 01:19:59.260
They wouldn't have some of the roles cast, and they would have writers read them.
有些角色还没定演员，他们就会让编剧来读。

1748
01:19:59.420 --> 01:20:05.100
And if a writer read a part, get ready, because Greg, there was a good chance Greg was going to put you in the show.
如果编剧读了某个角色，那就要做好准备了，因为格雷格很有可能会让你在剧中出演。

1749
01:20:05.100 --> 01:20:14.460
Well, he also told me that the look he gives to camera was actually him misunderstanding a piece of direction from Greg.
他还告诉我，他看向镜头的那个眼神，其实是他误解了格雷格的一条指令。

1750
01:20:14.700 --> 01:20:20.360
That Greg did not intend him to, like, perform that line to the camera as, like, a little joke.
格雷格本意并不是让他像开玩笑一样对着镜头说那句台词。

1751
01:20:20.360 --> 01:20:22.040
Like, oh, so that's where it went.
噢，原来它去那儿了。

1752
01:20:22.120 --> 01:20:23.700
He's talking about Meredith's uterus.
他在说梅雷迪思的子宫。

1753
01:20:23.800 --> 01:20:24.000
Yeah.
是啊。

1754
01:20:25.680 --> 01:20:27.420
But Greg left it in.
但格雷格把它留下了。

1755
01:20:27.540 --> 01:20:28.460
I liked it.
我挺喜欢的。

1756
01:20:28.700 --> 01:20:29.760
I liked it, too.
我也挺喜欢的。

1757
01:20:29.780 --> 01:20:31.320
But he said that was not the intention.
但他说是无心之失。

1758
01:20:31.320 --> 01:20:32.340
That was a mistake.
那是个失误。

1759
01:20:32.340 --> 01:20:45.400
Well, we learn in this scene that Meredith has been bitten by a bat, which we knew, but not only by a bat, but recently by a raccoon and a rat.
嗯，我们在这一幕里得知梅雷迪思被蝙蝠咬了，这点我们早就知道，但不仅是被蝙蝠咬，最近还被浣熊和老鼠咬过。

1760
01:20:45.640 --> 01:20:46.940
What the hell, Meredith?
搞什么鬼，梅雷迪思？

1761
01:20:47.520 --> 01:20:48.940
What is she doing?
她在干什么？

1762
01:20:49.320 --> 01:20:52.240
Honestly, a few of those animals could just live in her van.
说实话，其中几只动物完全可以直接住在她的货车里。

1763
01:20:52.780 --> 01:20:53.640
Meredith's van.
梅雷迪思的货车。

1764
01:20:53.820 --> 01:20:54.120
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1765
01:20:54.120 --> 01:21:00.160
Well, when Dwight comes back from the hospital, he fills Michael in on all of this.
嗯，德怀特从医院回来后，把这一切都告诉了迈克尔。

1766
01:21:00.360 --> 01:21:05.740
He says, you know, it turns out Meredith had been exposed to rabies.
他说，你知道，原来梅雷迪思接触过狂犬病毒。

1767
01:21:05.940 --> 01:21:07.380
Michael's like, ding, ding, ding, ding, ding.
迈克尔就像是，叮叮叮叮叮。

1768
01:21:08.260 --> 01:21:13.840
And that going to the hospital might have saved her life because she got a rabies vaccine.
而且去医院可能救了她的命，因为她接种了狂犬疫苗。

1769
01:21:14.040 --> 01:21:16.220
That is all Michael needed to hear.
迈克尔只需要听到这些就够了。

1770
01:21:17.080 --> 01:21:21.500
He hit her with a car and saved her life.
他开车撞了她，却救了她的命。

1771
01:21:21.980 --> 01:21:22.640
Yes.
没错。

1772
01:21:22.900 --> 01:21:30.960
Now, he also says in this scene, Dwight says, the only way to treat rabies is to start treatment before the symptoms start.
现在，他在这一幕里还说，德怀特说，治疗狂犬病的唯一方法就是在症状出现前就开始治疗。

1773
01:21:31.820 --> 01:21:33.260
Well, I looked it up.
嗯，我查过了。

1774
01:21:33.460 --> 01:21:33.780
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1775
01:21:34.260 --> 01:21:35.480
This is true.
这是真的。

1776
01:21:36.260 --> 01:21:43.360
Did you know, Angela, that nearly 100% of people who develop symptoms die from rabies?
安吉拉，你知道吗，几乎100%出现症状的狂犬病患者都会死亡？

1777
01:21:43.980 --> 01:21:44.640
Die.
死亡。

1778
01:21:45.340 --> 01:21:47.860
It cannot be cured once you get it.
一旦感染就无法治愈。

1779
01:21:47.980 --> 01:21:49.040
I did not know that.
我不知道这一点。

1780
01:21:49.640 --> 01:21:50.060
Yes.
是的。

1781
01:21:50.240 --> 01:21:55.320
So this is why you have to seek treatment immediately if you are ever bitten by an animal.
所以这就是为什么如果你被动物咬伤，必须立即寻求治疗。

1782
01:21:55.460 --> 01:21:57.440
And a lot of animals can carry rabies.
而且很多动物都可能携带狂犬病毒。

1783
01:21:57.540 --> 01:22:07.620
But since I looked it up, I'll let you know that in the United States, the most likely way to transmit rabies is through bats, coyotes, foxes, raccoons, and skunks.
既然我查过了，我就告诉你，在美国，传播狂犬病最常见的方式是通过蝙蝠、郊狼、狐狸、浣熊和臭鼬。

1784
01:22:08.620 --> 01:22:12.220
In Africa and Southeast Asia, it is stray dogs.
在非洲和东南亚，则是流浪狗。

1785
01:22:12.420 --> 01:22:13.420
I mean, what about monkeys?
我是说，那猴子呢？

1786
01:22:13.420 --> 01:22:19.220
There's parts of, like, Indonesia, like, if you go up to Ubud, like, there's monkeys, like, all over the place.
有些地方，比如印度尼西亚，如果你去乌布，到处都是猴子。

1787
01:22:19.340 --> 01:22:19.600
Any animal bite.
任何动物咬伤。

1788
01:22:19.760 --> 01:22:22.580
If you get bitten by any animal, just go.
如果你被任何动物咬了，就直接去。

1789
01:22:22.900 --> 01:22:24.760
Go get a rabies vaccine.
去打狂犬疫苗。

1790
01:22:25.200 --> 01:22:26.400
It also said—
上面还说——

1791
01:22:26.400 --> 01:22:27.420
What about squirrels?
那松鼠呢？

1792
01:22:28.580 --> 01:22:29.060
Yes!
是的！

1793
01:22:29.300 --> 01:22:30.240
Any animal.
任何动物。

1794
01:22:30.480 --> 01:22:32.260
If any animal bites you.
如果任何动物咬了你。

1795
01:22:32.260 --> 01:22:37.340
I'm just telling you the animals that are most likely to carry rabies in these locations.
我只是在告诉你这些地区最容易携带狂犬病毒的动物。

1796
01:22:37.340 --> 01:22:40.180
But any animal can give it to you.
但任何动物都可能传染给你。

1797
01:22:40.260 --> 01:22:41.460
Is a mongoose on the list?
猫鼬在名单上吗？

1798
01:22:43.100 --> 01:22:45.400
Is a mongoose any animal?
猫鼬算任何动物吗？

1799
01:22:47.220 --> 01:22:50.060
I'm just messing with you, but it's been really fun.
我只是在逗你玩，不过这真的很有趣。

1800
01:22:52.680 --> 01:22:56.480
Well, listen, here is the thing that I found most interesting.
好吧，听着，这是我发现最有趣的一点。

1801
01:22:56.480 --> 01:22:58.520
This is from the Mayo Clinic website.
这是来自梅奥诊所网站的内容。

1802
01:22:58.800 --> 01:22:59.900
Here's what it says.
上面是这样写的。

1803
01:23:00.080 --> 01:23:00.420
Okay.
好的。

1804
01:23:01.060 --> 01:23:03.740
If you wake up in the morning—
如果你早上醒来——

1805
01:23:03.740 --> 01:23:03.920
Okay.
好的。

1806
01:23:04.380 --> 01:23:06.220
—and there's a bat in your room—
——发现房间里有一只蝙蝠——

1807
01:23:06.220 --> 01:23:06.580
Okay.
好的。

1808
01:23:07.240 --> 01:23:09.100
—you should assume you've been bitten.
——你应该假设自己已经被咬了。

1809
01:23:10.040 --> 01:23:12.980
Because a bat can bite you without waking you up.
因为蝙蝠咬你时，你可能根本不会醒来。

1810
01:23:13.860 --> 01:23:21.920
It also said, if you find a bat by a person who can't tell you that they've been bitten like a child or an impaired adult,
上面还说，如果你在无法表达自己是否被咬的人（比如小孩或认知障碍的成年人）身边发现蝙蝠，

1811
01:23:22.180 --> 01:23:27.040
assume they have also been bitten and go get a rabies vaccine.
也要假设他们被咬了，并去接种狂犬疫苗。

1812
01:23:27.560 --> 01:23:30.480
Because once you show symptoms, there is no cure.
因为一旦出现症状，就无药可救了。

1813
01:23:31.020 --> 01:23:37.540
Well, I was watching an episode of Our Planet, and they were talking about these baby seals,
我之前在看一集《我们的星球》，他们当时在讲小海豹，

1814
01:23:38.160 --> 01:23:41.780
and there are vampire bats that go and try to just suck their blood.
有一种吸血蝙蝠会去吸它们的血。

1815
01:23:41.960 --> 01:23:43.100
And they can hop.
而且它们会跳。

1816
01:23:44.580 --> 01:23:45.580
They hop around.
它们蹦蹦跳跳的。

1817
01:23:45.940 --> 01:23:46.500
The seals are the bats.
海豹是蝙蝠。

1818
01:23:46.560 --> 01:23:47.520
The bats!
是蝙蝠！

1819
01:23:48.840 --> 01:23:49.680
They jump.
它们会跳。

1820
01:23:49.720 --> 01:23:51.060
I'm going to send you a video.
我要发个视频给你。

1821
01:23:51.260 --> 01:23:51.840
They hop.
它们会跳。

1822
01:23:52.100 --> 01:23:54.680
And they are bloodsuckers.
而且它们是吸血鬼。

1823
01:23:55.080 --> 01:23:56.360
They hop and bite.
它们又跳又咬。

1824
01:23:56.480 --> 01:23:57.220
They hop and bite.
它们又跳又咬。

1825
01:24:00.400 --> 01:24:00.820
Yeah.
是啊。

1826
01:24:01.320 --> 01:24:03.500
Well, there you go, guys.
好了，就是这样，伙计们。

1827
01:24:03.640 --> 01:24:04.140
There you go.
就是这样。

1828
01:24:04.140 --> 01:24:07.520
That's your rabies cheat sheet.
这就是你们的狂犬病速查指南。

1829
01:24:07.660 --> 01:24:09.900
That's everything you ever wanted to know about rabies.
这就是关于狂犬病你们想知道的一切。

1830
01:24:09.920 --> 01:24:12.620
Basically, if you get bit by an animal, that's what I learned.
基本上，如果你被动物咬了，这就是我学到的。

1831
01:24:12.760 --> 01:24:14.020
Get that rabies shot.
去打那针狂犬疫苗。

1832
01:24:14.760 --> 01:24:15.240
Good!
好！

1833
01:24:15.460 --> 01:24:16.200
Oh, yes!
哦，太棒了！

1834
01:24:16.200 --> 01:24:18.060
That was the takeaway I was hoping for.
这正是我希望大家得出的结论。

1835
01:24:18.060 --> 01:24:18.780
Well, there you go.
好了，就是这样。

1836
01:24:19.100 --> 01:24:23.240
Well, Michael is thrilled to find out that he has saved Meredith's life.
迈克尔发现自己救了梅雷迪思的命，感到非常激动。

1837
01:24:23.300 --> 01:24:23.620
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

1838
01:24:23.620 --> 01:24:24.920
He walks into the bullpen.
他走进办公区。

1839
01:24:25.080 --> 01:24:28.240
He declares that the curse has been broken.
他宣布诅咒已经被打破了。

1840
01:24:28.540 --> 01:24:30.240
Turns out there is a God.
事实证明上帝是存在的。

1841
01:24:31.800 --> 01:24:33.080
Everything is great.
一切都好起来了。

1842
01:24:33.080 --> 01:24:34.800
But who is Jesus' dad?
但耶稣的爸爸是谁呢？

1843
01:24:36.790 --> 01:24:37.270
Yeah.
是啊。

1844
01:24:37.390 --> 01:24:38.550
He's not sure, I guess.
我想他也不确定。

1845
01:24:39.190 --> 01:24:45.310
And meanwhile, Kevin, you know, has been on the case this whole episode trying to figure
与此同时，凯文，你知道的，整集都在调查，试图弄清楚

1846
01:24:45.310 --> 01:24:46.790
out if Jim and Pam are dating.
吉姆和帕姆是不是在约会。

1847
01:24:46.950 --> 01:24:50.090
He's positive that they are, but it's the end of the day.
他确信他们是在约会，但现在已经是下班时间了。

1848
01:24:50.170 --> 01:24:50.950
And he's like, you know what?
他心想，你知道吗？

1849
01:24:51.050 --> 01:24:52.370
I guess they're not together.
我想他们没在一起。

1850
01:24:52.370 --> 01:24:54.090
And now they probably never will be.
而且现在他们可能永远也不会在一起了。

1851
01:24:54.210 --> 01:24:57.910
And it's too bad because they're like PB and J.
真可惜，因为他们就像花生酱和果酱一样。

1852
